# CLIP ASSETS: LARGE ROM LIBRARY, SMALL REUSED DISPLAY BUFFERS
# Each movement BMP is a sheet of 6 columns by 7 rows of 160x144 pictures.
# background_clip(..., 160, 144) describes those picture dimensions in pixels.
# The compiler slices the sheet left-to-right, then top-to-bottom: frame 0 is
# top-left, frame 5 top-right, and frame 6 begins the next row. There are 42
# frames per movement, seven movements, and 294 prepared pictures overall.
#
# Frames 0..27 loop the main image; 28..41 dissolve toward the next movement.
# These full-screen pictures are prepared art, not live ray tracing. Each was
# authored with at most 72 distinct 8x8 patterns; repeated cells share patterns.
# The compiler converts the BMPs into ROM clip data and handles bank placement.
# At runtime draw_background uploads a chosen picture into a reusable inactive
# VRAM buffer. refresh_screen presents completed work safely. The entire sheet
# does not have to fit in VRAM, and no full-screen RAM pixel buffer is allocated.
#
# Paths are relative to this source file. The supplied assets are sufficient:
# building the demo does not require an asset generator. photons is different:
# sprite_sheet divides its small BMP into sprite cells for the live points.
# The clip and point sheet are separate layers with separate responsibilities.

# Frames run left-to-right, then top-to-bottom in each 6x7 BMP atlas.
# They reuse VRAM buffers at runtime; the whole animation need not fit in VRAM.
pulse = background_clip("../assets/movement-0.bmp", 160, 144)
iris = background_clip("../assets/movement-1.bmp", 160, 144)
inversion = background_clip("../assets/movement-2.bmp", 160, 144)
cathedral = background_clip("../assets/movement-3.bmp", 160, 144)
eye = background_clip("../assets/movement-4.bmp", 160, 144)
face = background_clip("../assets/movement-5.bmp", 160, 144)
signature = background_clip("../assets/movement-6.bmp", 160, 144)
photons = sprite_sheet("../assets/photons.bmp")
